From: DroidDeck
Subject: [PATCH] wayland backend: an unshown frame's buffer release is not an error

The nested backend pairs wl_buffer.release with its own Present(): a buffer the
compositor never attached logs "Compositor released us but we were not acquired.
Oh no." once per buffer at error level. But releasing a buffer that was committed
and then not shown is legal Wayland - the compositor only owes the buffer back,
and ours returns skipped frames' buffers immediately (frame limiter, occluded
surfaces, focus flips between the client and a game). A session that drops frames
then spams this line per buffer - 98 of them in one session.log - burying every
other message under a loop that looks fatal but is only bookkeeping. Debug level.

diff --git a/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
--- a/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/WaylandBackend.cpp
@@ -992,7 +992,11 @@
         }
         else
         {
-            xdg_log.errorf( "Compositor released us but we were not acquired. Oh no." );
+            /* DroidDeck: a buffer that was committed and never shown still has to
+             * come back, and our compositor returns skipped frames' buffers right
+             * away (limiter, occlusion, focus flips). Legal Wayland, not a fault -
+             * at error level one dropped frame per present buried the whole log. */
+            xdg_log.debugf( "Compositor released us but we were not acquired - an unshown frame's buffer coming back" );
         }
     }
 
